Let $v(x)=x^{^{{\scriptsize\dfrac23}}}$, then $[{u(x)}]^{^{{\scriptsize\dfrac23}}}=v\Bigl(u(x)\Bigr)$, or $(v\circ u)(x)$.

Therefore, the derivative of $[{u(x)}]^{^{{\scriptsize\dfrac23}}}$ can be found using **the chain rule**:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{d}{dx}[{u(x)}]^{^{{\scriptsize\dfrac23}}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[v\Bigl(u(x)\Bigr)\right]&&\gray{\text{Let }v(x)=x^{^{{\scriptsize\dfrac23}}}}
\\\\
&=v'\Bigl(u(x)\Bigr)\cdot u'(x)&&\gray{\text{The chain rule}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2}{3}[u(x)]^{^{-\scriptsize\dfrac{1}{3}}}\cdot u'(x)&&\gray{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[x^{^{{\scriptsize\dfrac23}}}\right]=\dfrac{2}{3}x^{^{-\scriptsize\dfrac{1}{3}}}}
\end{align}$
